course: dictionary
lesson: 15418
title: Sound words: sss
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are not real words at all. They are sounds written down so you can read them. «Sss» is a sound word, and it stands for the hissing noise a snake makes.
explain: Read the words around it to work out what it means. «The snake raised its head and went sss at the boy.» The snake is hissing, so sss is the hiss. It also tells you the snake may be angry or warning.
explain: You can also meet sss in phonics. Teachers say «sss» for the letter s, not «ess», so the sound is made like a hiss. Sss is a sound, not a real word, so you use it to show the sound itself.
fact: «Sss» is a sound word: a sound written down so you can read it.
fact: «Sss» is the hissing sound of a snake.
fact: «Sss» can also be the sound of air or steam escaping, or of something sizzling.
fact: In phonics, «sss» is how teachers say the sound of the letter s.
fact: «Sss» is similar to «shh» and «psst», which are used to get attention quietly.
exercise: «The snake went sss as it slid under the rock.» What is the sss? | A loud drum beat | *A snake hissing | A door slamming | A bird singing
exercise: «The kettle went sss as the steam escaped.» What does the sss show? | A dog barking | *Steam or air escaping | A baby crying | A car horn
exercise: In phonics, what sound does «sss» stand for? | The number six | The word snake | The letter t | *The letter s
test: Mum whispers, «Sss, the baby is asleep.» Why does she say sss? | To tell a joke | *To ask for quiet attention | To sing a song | To ask for loud music
test: Is «sss» a real word like «dog»? | Yes, it is a noun | *No, it is a sound written down, not a real word | Yes, it is a verb | No, it is a number
exam: The snake went «sss» in the long grass and the boy stepped back. What does sss tell the reader? | *It shows the snake is hissing and may be angry or warning | It shows the snake is singing | It shows the snake is asleep | It shows the snake is eating
